AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 2.2.1 (https://github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-FSR2, tag v2.2.1, commit
1680d1edd5c034f88ebbbb793d8b88f8842cf804), MIT licence (LICENSE.txt). Only the Vulkan backend and the shaders it needs
are kept. Unmodified except for the generated shader permutations.

shaders_vk/ holds the SPIR-V permutations generated with the SDK's own tools/sc/FidelityFX_SC.exe (glslang) from
ffx-fsr2-api/shaders/*.glsl by tools/fsr2_shaders.sh (Linux runs it under Wine, in a minute). To keep the size down only
the permutations the engine asks for are built: Analytic (reference) Lanczos reprojection (the LUT variant blurs on NVIDIA, which does not select it; both are built), motion vectors at render resolution and no jitter
cancellation are fixed; high dynamic range, inverted depth, sharpening and 16 bit maths stay selectable.
